  "note": "READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE ROWS. `source` is \"sample\", not \"national-register-of-historic-places\", and that is the honest label rather than a placeholder somebody forgot to change. AUTOMATED_HISTORIC_LANDMARK_IMPORT_SYSTEM.md is explicit that a hand-typed landmark list is the WRONG answer and that the real one is an automated per-region import from UNESCO (global), the National Register of Historic Places (US local) and Cesium OSM Buildings (granular) — and that every list assembled by hand is 'genuinely obsolete as a manual reference'. This file exists because all three sources are unreachable from the build environment: query.wikidata.org, whc.unesco.org and services1.arcgis.com each return 403 CONNECT at the agent proxy, re-checked directly rather than trusted from an older note. So this is the shape an import produces, filled with well-known public St. Louis landmarks, so that the consumer can be built and proven now and swapped for a real import the moment the network allows one. `significance` is an interpretive score on the engine's own 0-100 scale, not a figure any register publishes. Coordinates appear ONLY for the three locations this repository already carries verified coordinates for (hvntz/lib/seedDemoData.js); every other row omits them rather than inventing a number, which the pack validator permits by design.",
